<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN AMRO STARTS NUTRECO AS A BUY.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO STARTS NUTRECO AS A BUY.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Research note summary (10/07)</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>    Nutreco  Food and beverages   43.90   ABN AMRO Hoare Govett</p>
<p>COMMENT: (Buy) We initiate coverage with a Buy</p>
<p>recommendation and a target share price of NLG 55. Considering</p>
<p>the company is the largest value creator in its sector, its</p>
<p>current valuation, at a 30 percent discount to the market</p>
<p>and sector appears unjustifiably low. Returns on capital</p>
<p>employed are projected to further improve from 11.5 percent in</p>
<p>1996 to 16.7 percent in 2000. We expect interim results in</p>
<p>September...to trigger a revaluation.</p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS     P/E    P/CF   Dividend yield(%)</p>
<p>    1996 (actual)     2.05    21.6   7.2    0</p>
<p>    1997		  3.15    14.1   5.8    2.5</p>
<p>    1998		  3.50    12.7   6.1    2.8</p>
<p>    1999		  3.95    11.2   5.7    3.1</p>
<p>    2000		  4.40    10.1   5.5    3.5</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
